human trial applying a standardized topical formulation of alpha-terpinene to measure microbial clearance rates over two weeks.","eco":{"id":"ECO:0000180","label":"clinical study evidence"},"oxford":{"level":"2b","label":"individual cohort or observational study"},"evidence_lines":[{"design":"human_observational","eco":"ECO:0000180","papers":6},{"design":"animal","eco":"ECO:0007120","papers":2},{"design":"in_vitro","eco":"ECO:0000181","papers":12},{"design":"review","eco":"ECO:0000033","papers":2}]},{"claim_id":"cancer","area":"Cellular health","hypothesis":"Early observational work points toward a potential role in cellular protection, and scientists are investigating if it influences the behavior of abnormal cells.","evidence_level":"human_observational","paper_count":9,"study_to_test_it":"A randomized, placebo-controlled clinical trial in humans to measure specific biomarkers of cellular proliferation and oxidative stress over a six-month period.","eco":{"id":"ECO:0000180","label":"clinical study evidence"},"oxford":{"level":"2b","label":"individual cohort or observational study"},"evidence_lines":[{"design":"human_observational","eco":"ECO:0000180","papers":5},{"design":"animal","eco":"ECO:0007120","papers":4}]},{"claim_id":"pain","area":"Neuropathic pain","hypothesis":"Animal models suggest it might modulate pain pathways, and researchers are eager to see if this translates to soothing neuropathic discomfort in humans.","evidence_level":"animal","paper_count":3,"study_to_test_it":"A phase 1/2 human clinical trial evaluating the safety and efficacy of a topical alpha-terpinene preparation on self-reported pain scales in patients with peripheral neuropathy over four weeks.","eco":{"id":"ECO:0007120","label":"animal model system study evidence"},"oxford":{"level":"5","label":"bench or animal research"},"evidence_lines":[{"design":"animal","eco":"ECO:0007120","papers":3}]},{"claim_id":"neuroprotection","area":"Neurological health","hypothesis":"Early animal work points toward a neuroprotective effect, raising the exciting question of whether it could help shield the nervous system from stress or injury.","evidence_level":"animal","paper_count":1,"study_to_test_it":"A first-in-human pilot study measuring cerebrospinal fluid biomarkers of oxidative stress and neuronal health following controlled administration of alpha-terpinene over a 12-week period.","eco":{"id":"ECO:0007120","label":"animal model system study evidence"},"oxford":{"level":"5","label":"bench or animal research"},"evidence_lines":[{"design":"animal","eco":"ECO:0007120","papers":1}]}],"associated_conditions":[{"condition":"Solvents, acute toxic effect","mondo_id":null,"relationship":"recorded as an occupational exposure hazard in industrial settings"}],"cautions":"In industrial or highly concentrated solvent forms, alpha-terpinene is recognized as an occupational exposure hazard, though this is distinct from dietary consumption.","evidence_at_a_glance":"Best evidence so far is an individual randomised human trial (Oxford level 1b) for its antioxidant potential; most of the rest is human observational, animal, and lab research."}}
